{"timestamp": 1779360547.954376, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 11, "data": {"caller": "player_1", "reason": "Bob reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "medbay", "victim_name": "Charlie"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779360547.955023, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 11, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779360560.1142771, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I found Charlie\u2019s body in medbay, right where the scan area is. My route was weapons \u2192 security \u2192 electrical \u2192 medbay. I saw Diana in security around ticks 2 and 3, then I saw her leave security toward weapons at tick 4. I didn\u2019t see anyone else near medbay before I got there. Not hard accusing yet, just giving info."}}
{"timestamp": 1779360578.981052, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I started in security, went to weapons, then back to security. I saw Bob in security around ticks 2, 3, and 4. I never went to medbay and I never saw Charlie at all this round. I also didn\u2019t see Alice, Eve, or Frank on my route.\n\nSmall note: Bob says I left security toward weapons at tick 4, but from my view I still saw Bob in security at tick 4 too, so he was definitely there with me around then. Not accusing Bob just for reporting, but since the body was in medbay and I didn\u2019t see anyone else, I want to hear where Alice/Eve/Frank were."}}
{"timestamp": 1779360597.106733, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I started upper engine, went to oxygen, back through upper engine, then ended in lower engine. I saw Charlie alive in upper engine at ticks 2, 3, and 4 \u2014 he had come in from oxygen at tick 1. I never went into medbay and I didn\u2019t see the body.\n\nOnly other movement I saw was Frank leaving upper engine toward oxygen around tick 9. I didn\u2019t see Alice at all, and I didn\u2019t see Bob or Diana on my route. Since Charlie was last alive near upper engine, medbay is pretty close from there, so I\u2019d like to hear from Frank and Alice especially."}}
{"timestamp": 1779360618.4064379, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I started in lower engine, went up to upper engine, then left toward oxygen. I saw Eve in upper engine at ticks 8 and 9 \u2014 from my view she entered upper engine from oxygen at tick 8. I did not see Charlie at all, and I never went to medbay. I also didn\u2019t see Alice, Bob, or Diana.\n\nEve is right that she saw me leaving upper engine toward oxygen around tick 9, but I want to point out that puts me away from medbay at the end. The key info to me is Eve says Charlie was alive in upper engine ticks 2-4, and then the body ended up in medbay, which is close to upper engine. So the killer could be someone who moved through that upper engine/medbay area after tick 4.\n\nRight now Alice is the biggest unknown because nobody has placed her anywhere. Eve also has the last confirmed sighting of Charlie, so I want to hear Alice\u2019s route before deciding."}}
{"timestamp": 1779360693.260926, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I'll be upfront since I'm the unknown here. My route was electrical \u2192 medbay \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 weapons. I was in medbay around tick 7, and I actually saw Charlie come into medbay from upper engine at tick 7. He was alive when I left \u2014 I moved on to cafeteria and then ended in weapons, which is where I was when Bob called the meeting.\n\nSo that lines up with Eve's timeline: Charlie was in upper engine ticks 2-4, then came to medbay at tick 7. The question is who else was in or near medbay after I left.\n\nA couple things stand out to me:\n- Bob's route ends in medbay where he found the body. That's normal for a reporter, but it does mean he was the last one confirmed in that room.\n- Bob and Diana are basically each other's alibis in security/weapons area, so if one of them is lying, the other's story gets shaky too.\n- Frank came through upper engine late (tick 8-9), which is right next to medbay timing-wise.\n\nI don't think Eve did it \u2014 she was tracked in upper/lower engine and oxygen the whole time by Frank. Frank's the one whose path could swing into medbay after I left. I'm leaning Frank or Bob, but I want to hear reactions before locking in a vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1779360717.837762, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I want to push back a bit on Alice\u2019s framing. Alice is the only person who admits being in medbay with Charlie alive around tick 7, and nobody else has verified her path. I reported at medbay later, but I came from security \u2192 electrical \u2192 medbay and didn\u2019t see Alice leaving.\n\nDiana and I can place each other on the right side early. Eve and Frank also kind of place each other around upper/oxygen late. Alice is the only one who puts herself at the body location with the victim and then says she left him alive.\n\nFor me, Alice is the most suspicious right now."}}
{"timestamp": 1779360742.576013, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I can only really confirm Bob and my own path: we were together/near each other in security early, ticks 2-4, and I never went near medbay. So from my view, the important window is after Charlie was seen alive.\n\nAlice says Charlie was alive in medbay around tick 7, and Bob says he came security \u2192 electrical \u2192 medbay and found the body. That puts the kill pretty late and in medbay. Frank being in upper engine around tick 8-9 is near medbay, but Eve saw him going toward oxygen, which is the opposite direction.\n\nRight now I think the strongest suspicion is between Alice and Bob, because Alice admits being with Charlie alive in medbay, and Bob is the reporter arriving there after. I\u2019m less convinced on Frank unless someone can place him actually going toward medbay. Bob is right that Alice is the only one admitting direct contact with Charlie in medbay, but Bob also had the route to get there after leaving security. I\u2019m leaning Alice slightly over Bob, but I\u2019m not 100% locked."}}
{"timestamp": 1779360770.4722319, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I want to restate my info since it matters for the timing: I was upper engine \u2192 oxygen \u2192 upper engine \u2192 lower engine. I saw Charlie alive in upper engine ticks 2, 3, and 4, and I saw Frank leaving upper engine toward oxygen around tick 9. I never went medbay.\n\nGiven Alice says Charlie was alive in medbay at tick 7, that makes the kill window after that. Frank being in upper engine and then going oxygen at tick 9 makes me less suspicious of him \u2014 that\u2019s away from medbay, not toward it.\n\nSo to me it\u2019s mostly Alice vs Bob. Bob reported, but Alice is the one who admits being in medbay with Charlie alive and nobody can confirm she actually left him alive. Bob\u2019s route to medbay is also possible, but Diana at least places him earlier on the right side.\n\nI\u2019m leaning Alice right now unless Frank has something that changes the timing."}}
{"timestamp": 1779360792.4904351, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I don\u2019t have anything new beyond what I said: I was lower engine \u2192 upper engine \u2192 oxygen, and Eve saw me leaving upper engine toward oxygen around tick 9. I never went medbay and never saw Charlie.\n\nBased on everyone\u2019s info, I agree this is mostly Alice vs Bob. But Alice is the only one who says she was actually in medbay with Charlie alive, and nobody can verify that he was alive when she left. Bob reporting could be self-report, but Alice being the last admitted person with Charlie is stronger to me.\n\nAlso Alice trying to include me feels a bit convenient, because my movement was away from medbay and Eve can back that up. I\u2019m leaning Alice unless there\u2019s a big contradiction before voting."}}
{"timestamp": 1779360928.895929, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I hear you all, and I get why I'm the easy target \u2014 I put myself in the room. But think about it: if I killed Charlie at tick 7, why would I volunteer that I was in medbay with him? I could have just said \"electrical \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 weapons\" and skipped medbay entirely. Nobody saw me there. I told you because it's the truth and I'd rather give real info than get caught in a lie later.\n\nBob's route ends at the body. That's the classic self-report setup \u2014 kill, walk one room over, \"find\" the body. And Diana only confirms Bob in security ticks 2-4, which is exactly the early window. After tick 4, Bob's path through electrical \u2192 medbay is unverified by anyone. That's the same gap you're accusing me of.\n\nFrank, I'm not \"conveniently\" including you \u2014 Eve placed you in upper engine at tick 8-9, which is one room from medbay. You going to oxygen is Eve's claim, but the timing puts you adjacent to the kill room right after Charlie left it. I'm not hard-pushing you, just noting it's not as clean as you're making it sound.\n\nMy read is still Bob. He has the route, the arrival timing, and the reporter position. I'm voting Bob."}}
